; Tile set hg (2x2) and screen bank levels in the export format of the tile editor (concept, appendix A), but here generated by
; tools/gen_tiles_demo.py (the data is made up, no image content).
;
; Tile set hg: 6 tiles, each 2x2 character cells in size.
;   hg_c0..hg_c3  one table per cell (planar): index = tile number, value = screen code of cell k; cells row by row (k = row * 2 + column)
;   hg_col         color RAM byte per tile (TED color value: hue + 16 * luminance)
;   hg_props       property byte per tile (made-up example values; P_SOLID = 1 is one bit of it)
;   hg_tw, hg_th, hg_count  width and height in cells and number of tiles
; Screen bank levels: 3 maps (levels_map0..2), each levels_tiles_w x levels_tiles_h bytes row by row with tile numbers;
;   levels_screens is the address table (first all low bytes, then all high bytes: .lohifill); lv1_id..lv3_id are the screen numbers 0..2.

hg_c0:  .byte $11,$18,$1f,$26,$2d,$34
hg_c1:  .byte $14,$1b,$22,$29,$30,$37
hg_c2:  .byte $17,$1e,$25,$2c,$33,$3a
hg_c3:  .byte $1a,$21,$28,$2f,$36,$3d
hg_col:  .byte $71,$42,$55,$6f,$5d,$3e
hg_props:  .byte $00,$01,$01,$02,$04,$05
.const hg_tw = 2
.const hg_th = 2
.const hg_count = 6
.const P_SOLID = 1

